<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Each aircraft engine's own fuel and oil (Framework 0.360.0; docs/development/vehicle-standard.md, batch 3, VS6 and VS7). Not yet tested
    in game. The owner's cards of 27 Nov 2026: each engine its own pumps and oil; real consequences in the air, behind a setting that starts
    on ("Fuel and oil faults stop aircraft engines"); jet fuel freezing at its real point.

    Every aircraft (the aircraft loadout) gets both. Each engine gets its own fuel pump and oil pump, parts appended beside it
    (partPerEngine; EnginePumps.cs). What each engine's pumps and sump do is worked out in code (EngineFeeds.cs), because a system's
    figure is one for the whole vehicle: the readings here are the worst engine's, so the dashboard, the stages, the launch check and the
    service read the engine that needs it, and the Systems tab shows each engine's own under the row.

    Sources and labels:
    - Thresholds (a pump under a tenth starves its engine, under half gives three quarters; oil pressure gone under 0.15, low under 0.45;
      the oil level's pressure curve; a seizure in about five hours without pressure; 0.15 % of a sump burned an hour at full output) are
      the land fuel and lubrication systems' (Systems_Lubrication.xml), all authored, so a truck and an aircraft read alike.
    - Jet A-1's freezing point is -47 °C at most (its specifications, DEF STAN 91-091 and ASTM D1655; secondary: Wikipedia, "Jet fuel").
      Every aircraft in our loadouts burns jet fuel through a gas turbine. The fuel is taken as frozen solid 10 °C below that (authored:
      real fuel stays pumpable a little below its freezing point, wax crystals forming), and the engines stop half way, at -52 °C.
    - The fuel in the tanks follows the air it meets at 0.5 an hour (authored: a few hours aloft for a full wing to cool through).
    - The air at a cruising height: the standard atmosphere's fall of 6.5 °C a kilometre from the ground's own air, to 11 km (AirRule),
      never below -80 °C (authored), warmed by the ram rise of the air meeting the aircraft (total air temperature, T × 0.2 M², the
      standard formula for air): at Mach 0.7 for a fixed wing and 0.2 for a helicopter (authored typical cruising speeds; about +20 °C and
      +2 °C at -55 °C).
    - Hits: a hit engine loses 0.6 of its sump for each share of its health lost, a hit oil pump 0.25 (the land system's shares).
  -->
  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>
    <defName>PhobosVehicleSystem_EngineFuel</defName>
    <label>engine fuel feed</label>
    <description>Each engine's own fuel pump, and the fuel in the tanks. A ruined pump starves its engine, which stops; a damaged one feeds it poorly. Flying high and long in deep cold, the fuel cools toward the air it meets: below about -52 °C it no longer flows, and every engine stops.</description>
    <roles>
      <li>FuelPump</li>
      <li>Engine</li>
    </roles>
    <partPerEngine>
      <role>FuelPump</role>
      <add>
        <key>PhobosEngineFuelPump</key>
        <label>fuel pump</label>
        <eachLabel>{PART} fuel pump</eachLabel>
        <health>15</health>
        <depth>Internal</depth>
        <hitWeight>0.05</hitWeight>
        <hitWeightCE>2</hitWeightCE>
        <countsTowardDestruction>false</countsTowardDestruction>
      </add>
    </partPerEngine>
    <parameters>
      <fuelFollowRate>0.5</fuelFollowRate>
      <cruiseMach>0.7</cruiseMach>
      <rotorMach>0.2</rotorMach>
      <!-- Framework 0.365.0: what the fuel filter gains in an hour at full load on clean fuel (authored). -->
      <fuelFilterPerHour>0.01</fuelFilterPerHour>
    </parameters>
    <quantities>
      <li>
        <name>fuelFeed</name>
        <description>Fuel reaching the engines, the worst engine's pump. Ruined, that engine is starved and stops; weak, it gives three quarters.</description>
        <telltale>Phobos/VehicleSystems/Dash/Fuel</telltale>
        <label>fuel feed</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <derivedFrom>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineFeed">
            <reading>fuelFeed</reading>
          </li>
        </derivedFrom>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>0.1</to>
            <label>an engine starved</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_RefuseLaunch">
                <reason>PhobosVehicleSystems_RefuseLaunchEnginePump</reason>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting">
                  <setting>aircraftEngineFaults</setting>
                </when>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.1</from>
            <to>0.5</to>
            <label>weak</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>fuelTemperature</name>
        <description>The fuel in the tanks, which cools or warms toward the air it meets: high and fast, the cold air at height warmed a little by the speed.</description>
        <telltale>Phobos/VehicleSystems/Dash/Fuel</telltale>
        <label>fuel</label>
        <unit>Celsius</unit>
        <min>-80</min>
        <max>80</max>
        <startsAt>Ambient</startsAt>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>-40</to>
            <label>near freezing</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>fuelFrozen</name>
        <description>How far the jet fuel has frozen: from nothing at its freezing point, -47 °C, to solid at -57 °C. Half way, it no longer flows and every engine stops.</description>
        <telltale>Phobos/VehicleSystems/Dash/Fuel</telltale>
        <label>fuel frozen</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <hidden>true</hidden>
        <derivedFrom>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Quantity">
            <quantity>fuelTemperature</quantity>
            <curve>
              <points>
                <li>(-57, 1)</li>
                <li>(-47, 0)</li>
              </points>
            </curve>
          </li>
        </derivedFrom>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <from>0.5</from>
            <label>frozen</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_RefuseLaunch">
                <reason>PhobosVehicleSystems_RefuseLaunchFuelFrozen</reason>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting">
                  <setting>aircraftEngineFaults</setting>
                </when>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- Framework 0.365.0 (docs/development/vehicle-fuel-filter.md): one fuel filter for the aircraft, as on land, its harm worked out
             per engine in code (EngineFeeds, FuelFilterRule): clogged, every engine gives three quarters; blocked, with "Blocked fuel
             filters stop engines" and "Fuel and oil faults stop aircraft engines" on, every engine stops. These stages light the lamps. -->
        <name>fuelFilter</name>
        <description>How clogged the fuel filter is. Fuel burned clogs it slowly and stale fuel quickly; clogged, it feeds the engines poorly until the engine service changes it.</description>
        <telltale>Phobos/VehicleSystems/Dash/Fuel</telltale>
        <label>fuel filter</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <min>0</min>
        <max>1</max>
        <startsAt>Empty</startsAt>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <from>0.5</from>
            <to>0.7</to>
            <label>dirty</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgFuelFilterDirty</message>
                <type>CautionInput</type>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting"><setting>fuelFilters</setting></when>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.7</from>
            <to>0.95</to>
            <label>clogged</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgFuelFilterClogged</message>
                <type>CautionInput</type>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting"><setting>fuelFilters</setting></when>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.95</from>
            <label>blocked</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_RefuseLaunch">
                <reason>PhobosVehicleSystems_RefuseFuelFilter</reason>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting"><setting>fuelFilterStarves</setting></when>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- Framework 0.365.0 (FF5): how dirty the fuel aboard is, 0 clean to 1, kept by FuelDirt: fuel from a stale depot brings dirt, any
             other fuel thins it. -->
        <name>fuelDirt</name>
        <description>How dirty the fuel aboard is. Fuel from a stale depot is dirty; fresh fuel thins it.</description>
        <label>fuel dirt</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <min>0</min>
        <max>1</max>
        <startsAt>Empty</startsAt>
        <hidden>true</hidden>
      </li>
    </quantities>
    <flows>
      <li>
        <!-- Framework 0.365.0 (FF2): the filter clogs with the engine's load, a stand-in for the fuel through it, at 0.01 a full-load hour
             (authored: about 250 running hours at a usual 40 % load, every second engine service), five times as fast on wholly dirty fuel. -->
        <name>filterClogging</name>
        <quantity>fuelFilter</quantity>
        <kind>Into</kind>
        <factorParameter>fuelFilterPerHour</factorParameter>
        <inputs>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Setting"><setting>fuelFilters</setting></li>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineLoad" />
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Quantity">
            <quantity>fuelDirt</quantity>
            <curve>
              <points>
                <li>(0, 1)</li>
                <li>(1, 5)</li>
              </points>
            </curve>
          </li>
        </inputs>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>followAir</name>
        <quantity>fuelTemperature</quantity>
        <kind>Toward</kind>
        <target Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_FuelAir" />
        <factorParameter>fuelFollowRate</factorParameter>
      </li>
    </flows>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>

  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>
    <defName>PhobosVehicleSystem_EngineOil</defName>
    <label>engine oil</label>
    <description>Each engine's own sump and oil pump. A running engine burns a little oil, more when worn; a hit on an engine or its oil pump loses some. With no oil pressure a running engine seizes in a few hours; low, it wears. A service tops every sump up.</description>
    <roles>
      <li>OilPump</li>
      <li>Engine</li>
    </roles>
    <partPerEngine>
      <role>OilPump</role>
      <add>
        <key>PhobosEngineOilPump</key>
        <label>oil pump</label>
        <eachLabel>{PART} oil pump</eachLabel>
        <health>15</health>
        <depth>Internal</depth>
        <hitWeight>0.05</hitWeight>
        <hitWeightCE>2</hitWeightCE>
        <countsTowardDestruction>false</countsTowardDestruction>
      </add>
    </partPerEngine>
    <parameters>
      <oilBurnPerHour>0.0015</oilBurnPerHour>
      <seizeSharePerHour>0.2</seizeSharePerHour>
      <lowPressureWearPerHour>2</lowPressureWearPerHour>
      <engineHitOilPerShare>0.6</engineHitOilPerShare>
      <pumpHitOilPerShare>0.25</pumpHitOilPerShare>
    </parameters>
    <quantities>
      <li>
        <!-- The lowest sump, written by EngineFeeds each update; the service's top-up and its low-oil call read it as on land. -->
        <name>oilLevel</name>
        <description>How full the engines' sumps are, the emptiest one. A working engine burns a little, a worn one more.</description>
        <telltale>Phobos/VehicleSystems/Dash/OilLevel</telltale>
        <showOnDashboard>true</showOnDashboard>
        <label>oil level</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <min>0</min>
        <max>1</max>
        <startsAt>Full</startsAt>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>0.5</to>
            <label>low</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgOilLow</message>
                <type>CautionInput</type>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>oilPressure</name>
        <description>Oil reaching the bearings, the worst engine's. It needs oil in that engine's sump and its own pump working.</description>
        <telltale>Phobos/VehicleSystems/Dash/OilPressure</telltale>
        <label>oil pressure</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <derivedFrom>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineFeed">
            <reading>oilPressure</reading>
          </li>
        </derivedFrom>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>0.15</to>
            <label>gone</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_RefuseLaunch">
                <reason>PhobosVehicleSystems_RefuseLaunchOilGone</reason>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting">
                  <setting>aircraftEngineFaults</setting>
                </when>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.15</from>
            <to>0.45</to>
            <label>low</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
    </quantities>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>
</Defs>
